+## v1.1 IDE workspace
+
+The frontend now has two modes in the top bar:
+
+### Editor
+
+- project file Explorer;
+- UTF-8 text editor with `Ctrl+S`;
+- optimistic file-conflict detection using SHA-256;
+- persistent terminal sandbox per session;
+- terminal network disabled by default;
+- terminal reset recreates the sandbox from the current host project.
+
+### Agent
+
+- Harness chat;
+- plan/policy review;
+- agent execution logs;
+- ChatGPT/OpenAI provider tab.
+
+### Workspace persistence
+
+The browser remembers the active session, project path, selected mode, recent workspaces and local chat transcript. After `F5`, Kernl resumes the session. If the Go backend was also restarted, Kernl transparently creates a new session for the remembered project path.
+
+### ChatGPT tab
+
+`HARNESS_PLANNER=openai` + `OPENAI_API_KEY` enables the fully automatic supported flow. In `manual` mode the ChatGPT tab provides context downloads, prepared prompt, external ChatGPT launch, and structured-plan paste/validation. Consumer ChatGPT web UI scraping/automated Output extraction is intentionally not part of the harness.
